  "description": "Non-comparison sorts and selection over primitive keys (LSD RadixSort for (u)int/(u)long/float/double with key+payload and key+index (argsort) forms, CountingSort for bounded key ranges, PartialSort quickselect / bounded-heap top-k), plus StringSort, a stable ordinal string sort (cached-key multikey quicksort), and KWayMerge, a stable loser-tree merge of sorted runs over spans or lazy sequences. Span-based, with caller-supplied-scratch overloads that allocate nothing. The package README documents where each one wins and where it does not. Part of the Celerity family.",
